WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.961
This December, Netflix is cooking up a buffet
with a little something for everyone, with

00:00:04.961 --> 00:00:09.450
both exciting originals and new blockbusters
like Avengers: Infinity War.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.600
And that's just the beginning.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.800
Here's a quick look at everything good coming
to Netflix in December 2018.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.800
Andy Serkis made a name for himself as the
motion capture juggernaut behind Gollum in

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.890
The Lord of the Rings, and he's gone on to
parlay that particular skill into a long run

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:28.430
behind the camera and special effects of some
of the biggest blockbusters of the era.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.550
With Mowgli: Legend of the Jungle, Serkis
will again be heard and not seen as both the

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.400
director and the voice of Baloo.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:39.380
This gritty origin story sees the jungle boy
Mowgli on a quest to discover who he really

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:39.900
is.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:44.340
Along the way, he'll face down not only the
vicious Sher-Khan, but also perhaps the greatest

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.460
threat of all: Humans!

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.120
Look for it on December 7th.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.940
On-screen gangster tales have ranged in locale
from old-world Sicily to early 20th-century

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:58.090
London to that most terrifying location of
all, modern-day New Jersey.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.350
But what about Canada, eh?

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:04.220
Well, good news: Bad Blood is storming the
streets of Montreal with a gritty dramatization

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:06.680
of real-life crime boss Vito Rizzuto.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:11.230
After spending years in prison watching his
hard-won empire fall to pieces before his

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:15.940
eyes, Rizzuto gets released and sets out to
retake his territory and exact revenge on

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.780
the competing gangs who killed his son and
father.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.580
Check it out when the first season premieres
on December 7th.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.740
Espionage and political intrigue are the names
of the game in this Australian series that

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:30.880
follows a small group of spies working in
the secretive central Australian base Pine

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.470
Gap — a real location.

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:36.990
Pine Gap weaves actual events into its fictional
narrative, blurring the line between high-stakes

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.200
drama and real-life consequences.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:44.120
Although the series already aired in Australia
starting in October 2018, Pine Gap is set

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:48.640
to hit Netflix globally on December 7th with
a first-season run of six episodes.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:49.380
Don't miss it.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:55.400
Netflix's musical documentary series ReMastered
is tuning up for its third entry, and if it's

00:01:55.409 --> 00:01:58.659
anything like the first two, it's bound to
hit all the right notes.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:03.620
In Who Killed Jam Master Jay?, audiences will
get an in-depth look at the circumstances

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:08.760
surrounding the unsolved shooting that took
the life of the iconic hip hop DJ in 2007.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.180
Take a look when ReMastered: Who Killed Jam
Master Jay?

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.180
Drops on December 7th.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:18.080
There's a lot to love in this high-stakes
Australian series, which follows two strangers

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:22.209
who accidentally wind up in the middle of
a criminal conspiracy and find themselves

00:02:22.209 --> 00:02:24.720
on the run from both the police and the bad
guys.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:29.620
Wanted packs its airtime with comedy, action,
and drama, and leaves you hungry for more

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.069
every time the credits roll.

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:35.370
And with only six episodes in each of the
first two seasons and four in the upcoming

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:38.520
third season you can be sure that not a minute
goes to waste.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:43.020
You can still catch up on the first two seasons
before the third season shows up on December

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:43.580
13th.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.540
If you haven't clocked in for Cuckoo yet,
now's a good time to start.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:51.830
The show centers on a proper British couple
whose daughter just spent a year abroad.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:55.330
When they pick her up from the airport, they're
dismayed to find that she's returned with

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:58.530
her lover a slacker hippie played by Adam
Samberg.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.860
"Well, here he is.”

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:01.820
“Sorry?”

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.040
"It’s an honor Ken, just a great great honor.”

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:12.349
After the first season, however, Samberg left
for other projects and was replaced by American-werewolf-in-London

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:14.530
Taylor Lautner for the rest of the series.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:18.870
Somehow, it all ended up working, and you
can check out the fourth season on December

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:19.360
14th.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:25.300
"Soon your body will be butchered by extraterrestrial
lasers, but our souls shall remain together

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.300
through cuckoo."

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:32.160
With Narcos, Netflix enthralled the world
with the story of DEA agent Steve Murphy and

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:37.020
his partner, Javier Pena, as they worked to
bring down the notorious Pablo Escobar.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:41.660
Now, Netflix is putting their true-crime touch
on the tale with Inside the Real Narcos.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:46.500
As the name suggests, this docuseries will
delve into the real-life stories of drug cartels

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:49.490
in Latin America, told through interviews
with real criminals.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:53.920
It's sure to be an engaging experience, and
you can get your fix when Inside the Real

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.100
Narcos drops on December 14th.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:01.840
English comedian Jimmy Carr hosts this upcoming
comedy panel show, which sees a group of comedians

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.320
sitting down to solve some of the social problems
plaguing the world.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:09.360
Each episode will see a different panel of
comedians tackling a different issue, lending

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:11.840
their trademark wit to possible solutions.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.340
Effective?

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:13.220
Probably not.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.100
But it should be good for a laugh, at the
very least.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.360
Tune in for The Fix on December 14th.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:23.059
Novelist John Grisham carved out a career
with his numerous best-selling courtroom thrillers,

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:26.080
many of which have in turn been adapted into
blockbuster films.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:29.820
He's sold more books about judges than the
guy who wrote the Book of Judges.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:35.280
With his 2006 book The Innocent Man, however,
Grisham took his time-tested formula and turned

00:04:35.289 --> 00:04:38.439
it on its head, writing a true-crime account
instead of fiction.

00:04:38.439 --> 00:04:42.720
The Netflix adaptation will feature John Grisham
and will dig into the case through a series

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.580
of interviews with people who were involved
in the case.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:47.220
Look for it on December 14th.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:52.499
Clearly, Netflix has been down under to pick
up a ton of Australian series, but their upcoming

00:04:52.499 --> 00:04:57.159
fantasy thriller Tidelands marks the streamer's
first true Australian original show.

00:04:57.159 --> 00:05:00.849
Tidelands centers on a criminal who heads
home to a small village on the Australian

00:05:00.849 --> 00:05:02.700
coast in pursuit of a quiet life.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:07.420
But she soon finds that the town is secretly
home to a group of supernatural beings called

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.200
Tidelanders.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:09.960
Dive in on December 14th.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:14.760
Netflix hasn't been shy about showing off
their upcoming thriller Bird Box, and for

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:15.360
good reason.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:20.640
Based on the 2014 book of the same name, Bird
Box stars Sandra Bullock as Malorie, a new

00:05:20.659 --> 00:05:25.590
mother whose world is turned topsy turvy when
people begin taking their own lives in bizarre

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:26.080
ways.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.620
It turns out that there's some kind of sinister
force at work — once you see it, you're

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:30.740
driven to madness.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:31.680
Madness!

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:36.680
With a premiere date of December 21st, Bird
Box's dark vision of the future will be here

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.180
just in time for Christmas.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:38.980
Happy holidays!

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:43.100
"Please don't take my children!"

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:48.700
Netflix's original stand-up releases for December
will be arriving in two parts.

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:53.349
The first, Vir Das: Losing It, debuts on the
11th and marks the Indian comedian's second

00:05:53.349 --> 00:05:54.580
special on the service.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:58.800
Das told Gulf News that the new special will
touch on global events as well as his own

00:05:58.800 --> 00:05:59.400
personal life.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:03.600
The second stand-up special this month sees
talk show host Ellen DeGeneres taking to the

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:08.020
stage for the first time in 15 years with
a comedy set called Relatable.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.480
Take a look when it drops on the 18th.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:14.999
The holidays are arriving with a bang this
year, as Netflix introduces a handful of high-octane

00:06:14.999 --> 00:06:15.999
action favorites.

00:06:15.999 --> 00:06:21.449
November sadly saw the removal of Hellboy
II: The Golden Army, but December 1st sees

00:06:21.449 --> 00:06:23.840
its predecessor, 2004's Hellboy, showing up.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:29.080
Also on the first, look out for Terminator
Salvation and the 1985 martial arts flick

00:06:29.089 --> 00:06:30.210
The Last Dragon.

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:34.849
On Christmas Day, unwrap Avengers: Infinity
War, the first part of Marvel's epic Phase

00:06:34.849 --> 00:06:39.680
Three culmination that has the scrappy Avengers
taking on the big bad Titan Thanos.

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:43.970
You'll also find a brand new selection of
dramatic films landing this month, such as

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:48.259
8 Mile, Meet Joe Black, and Seven Pounds,
all of which arrive on the first.

00:06:48.259 --> 00:06:52.550
After that, the 16th offers the chance to
check out Eddie Redmayne before he was Newt

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:54.400
Scamander in The Theory of Everything.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:59.460
Redmayne stars as Stephen Hawking in this
hard-hitting bio-pic about the acclaimed physicists

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:03.889
early years and his struggles to cope with
the gradual onset of Lou Gehrig's disease.

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:08.270
There's an eclectic mix of comedies hitting
Netflix this December, but they all have one

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:10.260
thing in common: they're hilarious.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:11.720
"What's the matter David?

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:14.800
Never taken a shortcut before?"

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:23.680
The Friday trilogy hits Netflix on the first,
alongside Shaun of the Dead, The Big Lebowski,

00:07:23.689 --> 00:07:27.469
and the Bill Murray-led spy spoof The Man
Who Knew Too Little.

00:07:27.469 --> 00:07:30.520
Finally, 'tis the season for blood and mayhem
this Christmas.

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:36.389
The first of the month sees the arrival of
1998's Bride of Chucky, John Carpenter's 1983

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:41.160
adaptation of Stephen King's Christine, and
My Bloody Valentine, that cheesy 3D slasher

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:44.480
from 2009 about people throwing pickaxes at
you.

00:07:49.719 --> 00:07:53.039
It'll be easier than ever to binge brand new
shows in the coming month.

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:57.709
On the third, dive into Blue Planet II, the
follow-up to the BBC's critically acclaimed

00:07:57.709 --> 00:07:58.710
nature series.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:03.250
The sixth of the month sees the addition of
the first season of Happy!, an offbeat SyFy

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:07.530
series about a mentally unbalanced hitman
who becomes friends with his daughter's imaginary

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:08.020
unicorn.

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:12.820
Based on the graphic novel by Grant Morrison
and Darick Robertson, Happy! is a visual treat

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:15.869
for anyone looking for a different sort of
comic book hero.

